<h1 id=3D"font-size">Font Size</h1>

<p>Use the <code>&lt;size&gt;</code> tag to adjust the font size of your te=
xt.</p>
<p>You can specify the new size in pixels, font units, or percentage.</p>
<p>Pixel adjustments can be absolute (<code>5px</code>, <code>10px</code>, =
and so on) or relative (<code>+1</code> or <code>-1</code>, for example). R=
elative sizes are based on the original font size, so they're not cumulativ=
e.</p>
<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<pre tabindex=3D"0" style=3D"position: relative;"><code class=3D"hljs langu=
age-mel">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">size</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs=
-number">100</span>%&gt;Echo &lt;<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">size</span>=
=3D<span class=3D"hljs-number">80</span>%&gt;Echo &lt;<span class=3D"hljs-k=
eyword">size</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs-number">60</span>%&gt;Echo &lt;<s=
pan class=3D"hljs-keyword">size</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs-number">40</sp=
an>%&gt;Echo &lt;<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">size</span>=3D<span class=3D"=
hljs-number">20</span>%&gt;Echo
</code><button class=3D"copy-code icon" title=3D"Copy" type=3D"button" styl=
e=3D"opacity: 0;">=EE=A5=A3</button><div aria-live=3D"polite" class=3D"sr-o=
nly"></div></pre>
